# SPA Content-Security-Policy in REPORT-ONLY mode (default until the LEAD decides D-7: enforce, or replicate the
# live site, which has none). Browsers log violations in the console; no report collector is configured.
# To enforce, set PP_CSP_MODE=enforce in prod.env and redeploy the edge.
# - script-src 'self': the Vite build has no inline script.
# - style-src 'unsafe-inline': Vue sets inline style attributes and index.html carries the splash <style>.
# - img-src: PP_CSP_IMG_HOSTS = space-separated https origins for article/banner images and video thumbnails,
#   e.g. "https://img.youtube.com https://cdn.example.my" (the origins in PUBLIC_ORIGINS). No bare https:.
# - This file is a template: only ${PP_*} variables are substituted at container start.
# - frame-src: the video embeds the SPA allows (VideoPlayerFrame: youtube, vimeo, dailymotion).
add_header Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: ${PP_CSP_IMG_HOSTS}; font-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self'; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.dailymotion.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'" always;
